vaporOS NuttX patch: rp2040-reset-bootsel-watchdog

Problem:   board_reset() could not reboot the RP2040 reliably, and could not
           enter the USB bootloader, so every flash needed a physical replug.
Evidence:  A core-only reset (SYSRESETREQ) leaves the flash in XIP-disabled
           state after the second-stage bootloader has run once; the chip then
           falls into BOOTSEL instead of rebooting the application.
Fix:       board_reset(1) calls the bootrom's reset_usb_boot() (found through the
           ROM function table, 'UB'), which gives `reboot 1` -> BOOTSEL for
           hands-free flashing (tools/rp2040-flash.sh). Any other value does a full-chip
           watchdog reset (PSM_WDSEL + WATCHDOG_CTRL trigger) which restarts cleanly.
Upstream:  PROBABLY, after discussion. The watchdog reset is a plain bug fix.
           Reusing the reset value 1 for "enter BOOTSEL" is a convention
           choice NuttX maintainers may want expressed differently
           (e.g. a dedicated boardctl reset mode).

Apply: git -C ../nuttx apply ../vaporOS/patches/nuttx/rp2040-reset-bootsel-watchdog.patch   (setup.sh does this)

diff --git a/boards/arm/rp2040/common/src/rp2040_reset.c b/boards/arm/rp2040/common/src/rp2040_reset.c
index e59d2d65d9..02cc726dc7 100644
--- a/boards/arm/rp2040/common/src/rp2040_reset.c
+++ b/boards/arm/rp2040/common/src/rp2040_reset.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include <nuttx/config.h>
 #include <nuttx/board.h>
 #include <nuttx/arch.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <arch/irq.h>
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_BOARDCTL_RESET
 
@@ -56,7 +58,36 @@
 
 int board_reset(int status)
 {
-  up_systemreset();
+  /* vaporOS: "reboot 1" drops into the ROM USB bootloader (BOOTSEL), so
+   * the board can be reflashed without touching the BOOT button.
+   */
+
+  if (status == 1)
+    {
+      typedef void *(*rom_lookup_t)(uint16_t *table, uint32_t code);
+      typedef void (*reset_usb_boot_t)(uint32_t gpio_mask, uint32_t flags);
+
+      uint16_t *table = (uint16_t *)(uintptr_t)(*(uint16_t *)0x00000014);
+      rom_lookup_t lookup =
+        (rom_lookup_t)(uintptr_t)(*(uint16_t *)0x00000018);
+      reset_usb_boot_t reset_usb_boot =
+        (reset_usb_boot_t)lookup(table, 'U' | ('B' << 8));
+
+      up_irq_save();
+      reset_usb_boot(0, 0);
+    }
+
+  /* vaporOS: the generic armv6-m up_systemreset() only resets the core
+   * (SYSRESETREQ). On the RP2040 that leaves the QSPI flash in XIP mode and
+   * the bootrom then drops into BOOTSEL. Do what pico-sdk's
+   * watchdog_reboot() does instead: reset everything except the oscillators
+   * via the watchdog (PSM WDSEL, then WATCHDOG_CTRL.TRIGGER).
+   */
+
+  *(volatile uint32_t *)0x40010008 = 0x0001fffc;  /* PSM_WDSEL */
+  *(volatile uint32_t *)0x40058000 = 1u << 31;    /* WATCHDOG_CTRL */
+  for (; ; );
+
   return 0;
 }
 
